Sibling of the foundation-key ticket, same round trip, opposite direction.

`serialize_from` diffs whatever config.yml holds against the code defaults and
stores the difference as overrides in refs/karr/config. After kanban-md has
loaded and re-saved the view, that file contains kanban-md's migrated shape:
version 10 instead of 1, plus its full statuses, classes and tui blocks written
out explicitly.

So the import records all of that as deliberate per-board overrides, when in
fact the user changed nothing. The board config grows a copy of another tool's
defaults, and karr can no longer tell an intentional override from a migration
artefact — the next time karr's own defaults change, the board will not follow
them because it now has a frozen copy.

Fix direction: import should reconcile against the ref config instead of
replacing it, and should ignore keys whose value equals the effective default.
That is the same mechanism the foundation-key ticket needs, so the two are
probably one change.
